1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,451
By the end of this video, ZEC will be on its way to your wallet. There are two ways to get it.

2
00:00:07,651 --> 00:00:17,017
Route one: swap crypto you already have, right inside Zodl. Route two: buy ZEC on an exchange and send it to your wallet.

3
00:00:18,517 --> 00:00:27,034
Route one. On the home screen, tap Swap. You can swap other crypto into shielded ZEC right inside Zodl.

4
00:00:27,384 --> 00:00:33,221
Shielded means the amount, the sender and the receiver are encrypted on the blockchain.

5
00:00:33,571 --> 00:00:38,300
The swap uses NEAR Intents, not a centralized exchange.

6
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:44,401
Route two. Buy ZEC on an exchange, then withdraw it to your wallet.

7
00:00:44,751 --> 00:00:53,740
Most exchanges only send ZEC to a transparent address. Transparent means public on the blockchain, like Bitcoin.

8
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:57,994
That is fine. Zodl will offer to shield it when it arrives.

9
00:00:59,495 --> 00:01:10,595
To find your address, tap Receive. Your Zcash Shielded Address starts with u1. Zodl shows a new one each time. They all lead to the same wallet.

10
00:01:10,945 --> 00:01:21,973
Below it is your Zcash Transparent Address. It starts with t1. If an exchange will not accept your u1 address, give it the t1 address.

11
00:01:23,473 --> 00:01:31,331
Now wait a little. New ZEC needs 10 confirmations, about 12 and a half minutes, before you can spend it.

12
00:01:31,681 --> 00:01:40,726
When it lands, Zodl shows Wallet Backup Required. You already wrote your words down. Follow the steps from episode 1.

13
00:01:42,226 --> 00:01:44,128
Tick Getting ZEC on the site.

14
00:01:48,726 --> 00:01:56,932
Next, episode 3: shielding, so your ZEC goes private. See you at zero-to-shielded.vercel.app.
